<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="CGF1_MWP_LMG_MagFed_T1">
		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type81_LMG_</defName>
		<label>Type 81 LMG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x39mm. 30-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.

The Type 81 is a Chinese LMG developed in the 1970s and 80s in an attempt to replace the Type 56 copy of the Soviet RPD then in standard service. Mechanically a hybrid of the AK and SKS designs, the Type 81 features the same receiver and shares most parts with the Type 81 assault rifle, massively simplifying the rather complicated logistics of the PLA before its adoption. The weapon served as the standard PLA LMG for approximately 20 years, only beginning to be replaced in the late 90s by the QBZ-95.</description>
